  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Sunday)\nIssued at 1136 AM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nThe subtropical ridge gradually expands westward across the\nsoutheast U.S. this week as a trough deepens along the west coast\nby Wednesday. This will result in the ridge axis remaining in the\nvicinity with the subtropical high center shifting to along the \nGulf Coast late in the week. With the ridge firmly overhead expect\ncontinued hot conditions with triple digit heat across much of\neastern Oklahoma and near triple digits elsewhere through the\nforecast period. The ensemble model trend has been for any late \nweek rain chances to shift more north with time as the ridge \nrepositions itself to the southeast. Therefore, continued\nworsening of drought and fire weather conditions are expected.   \nWith mid level height fields rising into the 95th+ percentile \nrelative to climatology by next weekend there are no real\nindications of relief in the near term.",
